{"reference":"Psalms 51","book":"Psalms","chapter":51,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Prayer That Speaks Honestly","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 51 presents confession as a direct address to God: the speaker names sin, asks for cleansing and renewal, and moves toward praise. It belongs to the Psalter’s wider range of faithful speech, where lament, confession, petition, trust, thanksgiving, and praise can all be brought before God rather than praise being the only permitted response.","verse_refs":["Psalms 51:1-19"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_051_d2b75b2563f60ecc40d987ec"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}